@e2e @e2e_image
Feature: An image generated by an earlier invocation is referenced in place in its project
  A two-step pipeline (t2i, human review, i2i) runs as separate gflow invocations. The
  reference image was generated by Flow in the very project the i2i targets, so it is
  already there: it is attached where it is, never uploaded again (#995). On
  flow.google.com this used to be refused with exit 36, because only an image produced by
  the CURRENT process counted as in the project (#913).

  Scenario: i2i --ref <uuid> of an earlier invocation's image, in its project, attaches it in place
    Given an image generated by an earlier gflow invocation in a project
    When a new invocation runs image i2i with that image's uuid as --ref in that project
    Then the invocation succeeds and saves one image
    And the reference was attached in place, with no upload
